WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.609
LinkedIn Profile.

2
00:00:01.889 --> 00:00:05.707
Day 82 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Career phase.

3
00:00:07.457 --> 00:00:08.481
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.761 --> 00:00:20.495
Today's goal: write a LinkedIn profile that tells recruiters in 10 seconds who you are and what you're good at, and learn to write connection requests, posts and messages that people actually answer.

5
00:00:21.845 --> 00:00:22.698
Part 1.

6
00:00:22.978 --> 00:00:24.258
The 10-second test.

7
00:00:25.508 --> 00:00:32.207
A recruiter looks at your photo, headline and the first 2 lines of your About section, then decides whether to read on.

8
00:00:32.487 --> 00:00:33.980
Get those three right first.

9
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.247
Step 1:

10
00:00:36.527 --> 00:00:41.989
Photo and banner: clear face, plain background, smiling; a simple banner about your work.

11
00:00:42.269 --> 00:00:43.186
Step 2:

12
00:00:43.466 --> 00:00:48.735
Headline: role + key skills + what you deliver (not just Software Engineer at X).

13
00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:49.933
Step 3:

14
00:00:50.213 --> 00:00:54.373
About: a short story: what you do, your best results, what you're looking for.

15
00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:55.613
Step 4:

16
00:00:55.893 --> 00:00:59.221
Experience: results with numbers, not a list of duties.

17
00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:00.461
Step 5:

18
00:01:00.741 --> 00:01:05.626
Skills, recommendations, activity: proof from other people, and signs you're active.

19
00:01:06.976 --> 00:01:07.851
Part 2.

20
00:01:08.131 --> 00:01:10.008
Headline: formulas that work.

21
00:01:11.258 --> 00:01:12.623
Here is a quick table:

22
00:01:12.903 --> 00:01:14.034
Weak, and Strong.

23
00:01:14.314 --> 00:01:16.277
Software Engineer at XYZ:

24
00:01:16.557 --> 00:01:23.618
Senior Backend Engineer, Java, Kafka, AWS, Building payment systems for 2M+ daily transactions.

25
00:01:23.898 --> 00:01:25.327
Looking for opportunities:

26
00:01:25.607 --> 00:01:31.175
Full-Stack Developer (React, Node.js), Open to Bengaluru and Remote roles.

27
00:01:31.455 --> 00:01:32.309
Fresher:

28
00:01:32.589 --> 00:01:39.138
Computer Science Graduate, Java and Spring Boot, Built a grocery delivery app as a final-year project.

29
00:01:39.418 --> 00:01:40.293
Tech Lead:

30
00:01:40.573 --> 00:01:46.290
Engineering Lead, Grew a team from 3 to 12, Microservices, reliability, mentoring.

31
00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.536
Part 3.

32
00:01:48.816 --> 00:01:50.928
About section: a simple template.

33
00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.055
Here is a template you can copy.

34
00:01:54.335 --> 00:01:58.623
I'm a role with X years of experience building what for whom or industry.

35
00:01:58.903 --> 00:02:02.765
Recently, I biggest achievement with a number, and second achievement.

36
00:02:03.045 --> 00:02:07.823
I enjoy the kind of problems you like, and I'm known for a strength others. mention.

37
00:02:08.103 --> 00:02:08.935
Skills:

38
00:02:09.215 --> 00:02:10.709
5 to 8 key skills.

39
00:02:10.989 --> 00:02:15.789
I'm currently open to or interested in type of role in location or remote.

40
00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.946
Feel free to reach out at email.

41
00:02:20.796 --> 00:02:21.671
Example.

42
00:02:21.951 --> 00:02:28.649
I'm a backend engineer with nine years of experience building high-scale systems for fintech and e-commerce.

43
00:02:28.929 --> 00:02:39.745
Recently, I led the re-architecture of a grocery checkout that cut failed orders by 60%, and I reduced our cloud costs by 35 lakh rupees a year.

44
00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:49.028
I enjoy turning messy, slow systems into simple, reliable ones, and I'm known for clear incident communication and mentoring new engineers.

45
00:02:49.308 --> 00:02:50.140
Skills:

46
00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.644
Java, Spring Boot, Kafka, PostgreSQL, AWS, system design.

47
00:02:54.924 --> 00:02:58.636
I'm open to Staff Engineer roles in Bengaluru or remote.

48
00:02:59.986 --> 00:03:00.903
Part 4.

49
00:03:01.183 --> 00:03:03.551
Experience: duties versus results.

50
00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.167
Here is a quick table:

51
00:03:06.447 --> 00:03:07.769
Duties, and Results.

52
00:03:08.049 --> 00:03:09.692
Worked on the checkout service.:

53
00:03:09.972 --> 00:03:15.284
Re-architected checkout with the outbox pattern, cutting failed orders by 60%.

54
00:03:15.564 --> 00:03:17.292
Responsible for code reviews.:

55
00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:23.033
Introduced review guidelines that halved review time (3 days, then 1.5 days).

56
00:03:23.313 --> 00:03:24.892
Handled production issues.:

57
00:03:25.172 --> 00:03:31.700
Led 20 plus incidents as incident commander; wrote post-mortems that removed 3 recurring failures.

58
00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:39.962
Use action verbs: built, led, launched, reduced, improved, migrated, automated, mentored, designed, scaled.

59
00:03:41.312 --> 00:03:42.272
Part 5.

60
00:03:42.552 --> 00:03:44.493
Writing messages people answer.

61
00:03:45.743 --> 00:03:48.218
Connection request (300 characters).

62
00:03:48.498 --> 00:03:50.375
Here is a template you can copy.

63
00:03:50.655 --> 00:03:54.431
Hi Neha, I enjoyed your talk on consumer lag at Kafka Summit.

64
00:03:54.711 --> 00:03:58.039
I'm working on similar. problems in grocery delivery.

65
00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:00.367
I'd love to connect and follow your work.

66
00:04:00.647 --> 00:04:01.479
Ashish.

67
00:04:04.329 --> 00:04:08.959
Why it works: personal, specific, short, and it doesn't ask for anything yet.

68
00:04:10.309 --> 00:04:11.631
Asking for a referral.

69
00:04:11.911 --> 00:04:13.789
Here is a template you can copy.

70
00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:15.775
Hi Arjun, hope you're well!

71
00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:19.362
I saw that Brightsoft is hiring a Senior Backend Engineer.

72
00:04:19.642 --> 00:04:22.607
(job ID 4471).

73
00:04:22.887 --> 00:04:30.077
I have 9 years in Java and Kafka, and I led a checkout re-architecture. that cut failures by 60%.

74
00:04:30.357 --> 00:04:32.213
Would you be comfortable referring me?

75
00:04:32.493 --> 00:04:36.610
I've attached my CV. and. a 3-line summary you can forward.

76
00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.066
Totally fine if not, thanks either way!

77
00:04:41.916 --> 00:04:43.409
Replying to a recruiter.

78
00:04:43.689 --> 00:04:45.567
Here is a template you can copy.

79
00:04:45.847 --> 00:04:47.788
Hi Riya, thanks for reaching out!

80
00:04:48.068 --> 00:04:49.583
The role sounds interesting.

81
00:04:49.863 --> 00:04:54.812
Could you share the. job description, the team I'd be working with, and the budgeted range?

82
00:04:55.092 --> 00:04:57.887
I'm currently. on a 60-day notice period.

83
00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:03.479
Happy to set up a call this week, Tuesday or Thursday. after 5 pm works for me.

84
00:05:06.329 --> 00:05:07.715
Saying no politely.

85
00:05:07.995 --> 00:05:09.873
Here is a template you can copy.

86
00:05:10.153 --> 00:05:12.137
Hi Riya, thanks for thinking of me.

87
00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:17.259
I'm not looking for a change right now, but I'd. be glad to stay in touch for the future.

88
00:05:17.539 --> 00:05:19.033
All the best with the search!

89
00:05:21.883 --> 00:05:22.821
Part 6.

90
00:05:23.101 --> 00:05:24.893
Posting: share without bragging.

91
00:05:26.143 --> 00:05:28.021
Here is a template you can copy.

92
00:05:28.301 --> 00:05:32.781
Our checkout failed 1,200 orders in 40 minutes last year.

93
00:05:33.061 --> 00:05:34.362
Here's what we changed.

94
00:05:34.642 --> 00:05:40.914
The cause: a payment SDK timeout of 2s, under a bank latency of 2.6s at peak.

95
00:05:41.194 --> 00:05:45.674
We fixed it with canary deploys, peak-hour deploy blocks and better alerts.

96
00:05:45.954 --> 00:05:50.434
Biggest lesson: the fix was 20% code and 80% process.

97
00:05:50.714 --> 00:05:53.957
How does your team stop risky deploys during peak traffic?

98
00:05:56.807 --> 00:05:57.553
Warning:

99
00:05:57.833 --> 00:05:58.495
Don't.

100
00:05:58.775 --> 00:06:11.361
Share confidential numbers, customer names or internal screenshots, criticise your employer, post only OpenToWork with no details, send a referral request to a stranger as your first message.

101
00:06:12.711 --> 00:06:13.650
Part 7.

102
00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:17.087
Conversation: networking message turns into a call.

103
00:06:18.337 --> 00:06:20.364
Here is how the conversation goes.

104
00:06:20.644 --> 00:06:22.692
Hi Ashish, thanks for connecting!

105
00:06:22.972 --> 00:06:24.551
Glad the talk was useful.

106
00:06:24.831 --> 00:06:26.047
It really was.

107
00:06:26.327 --> 00:06:29.463
We had the same consumer lag problem last month.

108
00:06:29.743 --> 00:06:32.111
Could I ask you one question about it?

109
00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:33.607
Sure, go ahead.

110
00:06:33.887 --> 00:06:38.367
Did you increase partitions, or change the consumer batch size first?

111
00:06:39.717 --> 00:06:41.317
The conversation continues.

112
00:06:41.597 --> 00:06:43.005
Batch size first.

113
00:06:43.285 --> 00:06:46.207
Partitions only helped after we fixed slow processing.

114
00:06:46.487 --> 00:06:48.621
That's exactly what I suspected.

115
00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:49.818
Thank you!

116
00:06:50.098 --> 00:06:52.871
Would you be open to a 15-minute call sometime?

117
00:06:53.151 --> 00:06:55.178
I'd love to hear how you scaled it.

118
00:06:55.458 --> 00:06:56.823
Happy to.

119
00:06:57.103 --> 00:06:58.725
How about Friday at 4?

120
00:06:59.005 --> 00:07:00.669
Friday at 4 works.

121
00:07:00.949 --> 00:07:02.485
I'll send an invite.

122
00:07:02.765 --> 00:07:03.959
Thanks, Neha!

123
00:07:05.309 --> 00:07:06.184
Part 8.

124
00:07:06.464 --> 00:07:07.381
Practice.

125
00:07:08.631 --> 00:07:15.479
Rewrite your headline using Role, Core skills, Result or domain, and write the first two lines of your About section.

126
00:07:16.829 --> 00:07:17.725
Part 9.

127
00:07:18.005 --> 00:07:19.051
Speak today.

128
00:07:20.301 --> 00:07:23.693
Update your headline and the first two lines of your About section.

129
00:07:23.973 --> 00:07:27.791
Rewrite one experience line from a duty to a result with a number.

130
00:07:28.071 --> 00:07:30.439
Send one personalised connection request.

131
00:07:31.789 --> 00:07:33.325
That's the end of this lesson.

132
00:07:33.605 --> 00:07:38.277
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

133
00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:44.659
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

